l=p.zm(A.c0(!0,!0,!1)+" are the main way to organize your ideas. Each "+A.c0(!1,!1,!1)+" represents a type of activity or interest.\n\nExamples of "+A.c0(!1,!0,!1)+':\n\u2022 "Watch a Movie"\n\u2022 "Read a Book"\n\u2022 "Try a Restaurant"\n\u2022 "Learn a Skill"\n\u2022 "Visit a Place"\n\nWithin each '+A.c0(!1,!1,!1)+", you add individual "+A.bb(!1,!0,!1)+' - the specific things you want to do. For example, in "Watch a Movie", you might add "The Godfather", "Blade Runner", or "Spirited Away".\n\nYou can make your '+A.c0(!1,!0,!1)+" public to share with others, or keep them private for your eyes only.\n",a,1,"Compiling "+l)
s=p.zm("You can add links to external resources for your "+A.bb(!1,!0,!1)+". This makes it easy to jump directly to relevant content.\n\nSupported link types:\n\u2022 Streaming services (Netflix, Amazon Prime, Apple TV+, etc.)\n\u2022 Music services (Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube Music, Tidal)\n\u2022 Websites and articles\n\u2022 Any other URL you want to save\n\nWhen you add a link, the app will try to automatically fetch information like titles and descriptions. For some services (like movies and music), it can even find where content is available to stream.\n\nPro tip: Just paste a URL into the headline when adding a new "+A.bb(!1,!1,!1)+", and the app will handle the rest!\n",a,2,"Linking Elsewhere")
r=A.bb(!0,!0,!1)
r=p.zm('On mobile, you can quickly capture content from other apps by using the Share feature.\n\nHow it works:\n1. Find something interesting in another app (a website, article, video, etc.)\n2. Tap the Share button\n3. Select "I\'ve Been Meaning To" from the share menu\n4. Tell the app what '+A.c0(!1,!1,!1)+" it pertains to\n5. The app will create a new "+A.bb(!1,!1,!1)+" with the shared link\n\nThis is a fast way to capture ideas on the go without switching apps. The shared content will be automatically added as a link to your new "+A.bb(!1,!1,!1)+", and you can organize it into the appropriate "+A.c0(!1,!1,!1)+" later.\n\nPerfect for saving articles to read, videos to watch, or anything else you come across while browsing!\n",a,3,"Turn Shares into "+r)
